  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "The Prophet ﷺ is never drawn or symbolised; footsteps only for «انقلبتم على أعقابكم», the gloss carrying the verse's condition «أفإن مات أو قتل». An hourglass for the appointed term, two_paths for the reward of this world or the next. 145:11-24 is not glossed: Al-Muyassar's wording there is in Allah's first person. STAGING v4: The Prophet is never drawn or symbolised (144:2-4 have no plate and no zoom). 144: believers in a prayer hall hold the Book that was brought to them (read), stay standing, nobody turns back (the turning back is conditional: only the footsteps plate, the gloss carries the condition), and pray on «الشاكرين» (Al-Muyassar: ثبت على الإيمان وشكر ربه; As-Sa'di: الشكر ... القيام بعبودية الله). 145: death by Allah's leave is not pictured (hourglass plate on 145:9); a rich man for those who seek the reward of this world (coins plate), believers raising hands for those who seek the Hereafter (Al-Muyassar: من يطلب بعمله ... عرض الدنيا / الجزاء من الله في الآخرة); no one is drawn giving, since the giver is Allah."
